{"id":"35b6cdd4-36b1-45be-8de8-09752f74b61a","object":"chat.completion","created":1785035801,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    min_sum = sum(s['minimum'] for s in segments)\\n    cap_sum = sum(s['capacity'] for s in segments)\\n    if budget < min_sum or budget > cap_sum:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget out of range')\\n    allocations = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\\n    remaining = budget - sum(allocations)\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        best_value = -1.0\\n        for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n            if allocations[i] < seg['capacity']:\\n                value = seg['importance'] / (allocations[i] + 1)\\n                if value > best_value:\\n                    best_value = value\\n                    best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            break\\n        allocations[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    by_name = {segments[i]['name']: allocations[i] for i in range(n)}\\n    return {\\n        'allocations': allocations,\\n        'by_name': by_name,\\n        'total': sum(allocations)\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce solve(case) that returns a JSON object with allocations (list of ints, same order as segments), by_name (dict mapping segment name to allocation), total (sum of allocations). The algorithm: allocate minimum to each segment first, compute remaining budget, then iteratively allocate one token to the segment that maximizes importance / (current_allocation + 1) (since next position is current+1? Actually \"importance divided by its next allocated position\" - next allocated position would be current allocation + 1. So importance / (current_allocation + 1). Tie break by original order. Continue until budget exhausted or all segments at capacity? But budget may be les