.\n\nReturn: allocations list, by_name dict: {seg['name']: allocations[i]}, total = sum(allocations).\n\nEdge: handling equal ratios: we iterate over segments in order, pick first max. Or use stable sort.\n\nImplementation: We'll write solve(case) function. Use Python standard library only.\n\nWrite code without mutation of case. Ensure we don't modify case.\n\nNow produce JSON with key implementation, value as string of Python source code, properly escaped.\n\nOutput only one JSON object.\n\nLet's draft code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    segments = case['segments']\n    budget = case['budget']\n    n = len(segments)\n    # Validate\n    min_sum = sum(s['minimum'] for s in segments)\n    cap_sum = sum(s['capacity'] for s in segments)\n    if budget < min_sum or budget > cap_sum:\n        # According to spec, reject. We'll raise, but to be safe maybe return zeros? Not specified. Raise.\n        raise ValueError(\"Budget out of range\")\n    allocations = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\n    remaining = budget - sum(allocations)\n    while remaining > 0:\n        best_idx = -1\n        best_value = -1.0\n        for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\n            if allocations[i] < seg['capacity']:\n                value = seg['importance'] / (allocations[i] + 1)  # next position\n                if value > best_value:\n                    best_value = value\n                    best_idx = i\n                # ties not handled? If equal, first encountered wins, which is stable tie break (original order)\n        if best_idx == -1:\n            break  # no room, but budget may exceed capacity? Already checked.\n        allocations[best_idx] += 1\n        remaining -= 1\n    by_name = {segments[i]['name']: allocations[i] for i in range(n)}\n    return {\n        'allocations': allocations,\n        'by_name': by_name,\n        'total': sum(allocations)\n    }\n\nThat's it. Ensure we don't mutate case. We are creating new allocations list.\n\nNow convert to JSON string. Escape